  "code": "import numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nt = np.arange(0.0, 2.0, 0.01)\ns = np.sin(2*np.pi*t)\n\nplt.plot(t, s)\nplt.text(0, -1, r'Hello, world!', fontsize=15)\nplt.title(r'$\\mathcal{A}\\sin(\\omega t)$', fontsize=20)\nplt.xlabel('Time [s]')\nplt.ylabel('Voltage [mV]')\nplt.show()\n",
  "prose": "Set the special text objects title, xlabel, and ylabel through the dedicated pyplot functions. Additional text objects can be placed in the axes using text. You can use TeX-like mathematical typesetting in all texts; see also Writing mathematical expressions. Gallery generated by Sphinx-Gallery",
